TypeScript compilation failed due to type mismatch in `ExtraButtonComponent.onClick()` callback at line 711 of `mobile-search-leaf.ts`. The callback signature expects `() => any` but was receiving `(event) => void`.

## Changes

- **Made event parameter optional** in `showMultipleFilesMenu(event?: MouseEvent)`
- **Added conditional menu positioning**: 
  - `menu.showAtMouseEvent(event)` when called from contextmenu handlers
  - `menu.showAtPosition()` at center screen when called from button click
- **Removed event parameter** from ExtraButtonComponent onClick callback

## Example

```typescript
// Before: Type error - onClick expects () => any
new ExtraButtonComponent(this.selectionCommandBar)
  .onClick((event) => this.showMultipleFilesMenu(event));

// After: Correct signature, optional event handling
new ExtraButtonComponent(this.selectionCommandBar)
  .onClick(() => this.showMultipleFilesMenu());

private showMultipleFilesMenu(event?: MouseEvent): void {
  // ... menu setup ...
  if (event) {
    menu.showAtMouseEvent(event);
  } else {
    menu.showAtPosition({ x: window.innerWidth / 2, y: window.innerHeight / 2 });
  }
}
```

Version bumped to 1.1.1 with changelog entry.

