## Summary

This PR fixes a clippy warning (`clippy::collapsible-if`) in `src/types.rs` by collapsing nested if statements in the throttle checking logic.

## Change

**Before:**
```rust
if let Some(duration) = throttle {
    if pr.was_comment_posted_recently(body, duration) {
        return false;
    }
}
```

**After:**
```rust
if let Some(duration) = throttle
    && pr.was_comment_posted_recently(body, duration) {
    return false;
}
```

## Benefits

- Eliminates clippy warning
- Improves code readability
- Follows Rust idioms for combining conditions

## Testing

- ✅ All unit tests pass
- ✅ Clippy checks pass with no warnings  
- ✅ Functionality unchanged

